example.code:
public sealed class PacketParseException : BaseException
{
    public PacketParseException(string message)
        : base(message) { }

    public PacketParseException(string message, Exception innerException)
        : base(message, innerException) { }
}

[Packet]
public sealed class PingRequest : PacketBase<PingRequest>
{
    public const ushort OpCodeValue = 0x1001;

    public PingRequest()
    {
        this.OpCode = OpCodeValue;
    }
}

member.remarks:
             This attribute is applied to classes containing methods that handle incoming packet commands.
             The methods in the target class must adhere to the following requirements to be compatible with the handler compiler:


Method Parameter Requirements:



             The method must have either 2 or 3 parameters.




             The first parameter must implement .
             This parameter represents the packet being handled.





             The second parameter must implement .
             This parameter represents the connection on which the packet was received.





             The third parameter (if present) must be of type .
             This parameter is used for cooperative cancellation of the handler execution.





Return Type:




             The method may return one of the following:


.

 (for asynchronous methods).

 (for lightweight asynchronous methods).



             A generic task ( or
             ), where TResult is the return type.








Access Modifiers:



             The method must be public.



             The method may be either static or instance-based, depending on the controller's design.




Error Handling:
             If the method does not meet any of the above requirements, the following exceptions may be thrown during the controller scanning process:




             : Thrown if the parameter count, types, or return type are invalid.





             : Thrown if multiple methods match the same operation code.





             Example of a valid controller with the required handler methods:

             [PacketHandler(name: "ExampleController", isActive: true, version: "1.1")]
             public class ExampleController
             {
                 // A handler with 2 parameters
                 public void HandleLogin(LoginPacket packet, IConnection connection)
                 {
                     // Handle the login logic here.
                 }

                 // A handler with 3 parameters
                 public ValueTask ProcessData(DataPacket packet, IConnection connection, CancellationToken token)
                 {
                     // Handle data processing logic here asynchronously.
                     return ValueTask.CompletedTask;
                 }
             }

